        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-1547] The EV shall adjust its nominal power level in such a way that it at no time exceeds the hard limits as defined by the boundaries of selected ChargingSchedule and — in BPT use cases — the DischargingSchedule. The EV shall ensure that required power ramp limitations are not violated during those adjustments. If the new limit for the power level is \"zero\", then the resulting active current flow shall be as close to \"zero\" as technically feasible. In cases where the EV violates any of those hard limits the EVSE may drop the EVs power connection and terminate the charging session.",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                1048,
                1053,
                1230
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 7,
